                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Seniors with Medicare Part D will see their out-of-pocket drug costs capped at $2,000 per year.\n\nThis means lower costs for more than 176,000 Rhode Islanders. Price should never prevent access to needed medicine. 4/8",
